# TUI-DESIGN-3 §4.4 F14: a `/` line while a submission is in flight (JEVCODE_MOCK_JEV_MS=1500 delays the mock decider, so the reply waits for the reading) is not dropped —
# `/status` answers while the request is in flight; the reply lands afterwards; /exit leaves 0
expect \x1b\[\?25l
expect Say hi
expect sess \$
sleep 0.3
send hi
sleep 0.2
send \r
expect thinking
send /status
sleep 0.15
send \r
expect \[ui\](?:\x1b\[[0-9;]*m)* status
expect \[jevcode\](?:\x1b\[[0-9;]*m)* Hi
send /exit
sleep 0.2
send \r
eof
